examples.question_text:
Identify each angle pair as corresponding, alternate or co-interior:
(a) $11$ and $15$
(b) $13$ and $16$
(c) $14$ and $16$.
The two crossed lines are not parallel.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-2.5,1.2)--(2.5,1.2);
\draw (-2.5,-1.5)--(2.5,-0.9);
\draw (-1.2,-2.4)--(1.2,2.4);
\node at (0.35,1.65) {$11$};
\node at (1.15,1.45) {$12$};
\node at (0.05,0.95) {$13$};
\node at (0.85,0.75) {$14$};
\node at (-0.95,-0.75) {$15$};
\node at (-0.15,-0.95) {$16$};
\node at (-1.2,-1.6) {$17$};
\node at (-0.4,-1.7) {$18$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
**Corresponding:** angle $28$ occupies the matching corner at the other intersection.

**Alternate:** angle $25$ is inside the lines and on the opposite side of the transversal from angle $24$.

**Co-interior:** angle $26$ is inside the lines and on the same side of the transversal as angle $24$.

The partners, in order, are $28$, $25$ and $26$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{pairblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{pairgreen}{HTML}{4F9B63}
\definecolor{pairpurple}{HTML}{8B5CC7}
\draw (-2.5,1.2)--(2.5,1.2);
\draw (-2.5,-1.2)--(2.5,-1.2);
\draw (-1.2,-2.4)--(1.2,2.4);
\draw (1.75,1.32)--(1.95,1.2)--(1.75,1.08);
\draw (1.75,-1.08)--(1.95,-1.2)--(1.75,-1.32);
\draw (0.6,1.2) ++(243.435:0.42) arc[start angle=243.435,end angle=360,radius=0.42];
\draw[pairblue,thick] (-0.6,-1.2) ++(243.435:0.42) arc[start angle=243.435,end angle=360,radius=0.42];
\draw[pairgreen,thick] (-0.6,-1.2) ++(63.435:0.42) arc[start angle=63.435,end angle=180,radius=0.42];
\draw[pairpurple,thick] (-0.6,-1.2) ++(0:0.55) arc[start angle=0,end angle=63.435,radius=0.55];
\node at (0.85,0.75) {$24$};
\node at (-0.85,-0.75) {$25$};
\node at (-0.05,-0.95) {$26$};
\node at (-0.35,-1.65) {$28$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Blue marks the corresponding partner, green the alternate partner and purple the co-interior partner.
